{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     footer-lesson — the footer a READING SURFACE gets.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     `abstract/02` names this as the counterpart to chrome/coursenav: the
     chrome swaps as a pair, so a lesson does not end in a four-column
     marketing footer with a newsletter form in it.

     A reader who has just finished a lesson wants exactly one thing — the
     next lesson — and giving them a site map instead is how a course loses
     people at the end of every page.

     STUBBED, HONESTLY. The previous/next pair needs Ghost's `{{next_post}}` /
     `{{prev_post}}` scoped to the lesson's own course, which needs the
     `#course-*` tag vocabulary in `abstract/18` to be settled and applied to
     real content. Until then this is the hairline and the copyright and
     nothing else — which is correct-and-plain rather than wrong-and-busy.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<footer class="ns-footer">
    <div class="ns-page">
        <div class="ns-footer__bar">
            <span>&copy; {{date format="YYYY"}} {{@site.title}}</span>
            <span class="ns-footer__spacer"></span>
            <a href="https://ghost.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{t "Published with Ghost"}}</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</footer>
